From 48eac19e39ad66a47fb43608b59f3928fb197aa4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LiBr <me@nvme0n1p.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:55:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 46/47] Z 6III: USB -- a device-mode DWC3, a host behind
 USB/IP, PTP from outside

The camera now enumerates on its USB-C port and answers PTP: with
-machine usbip=<socket | host:port>, z63-tools/ptp.py reads the device
info ("Nikon Corporation Z6_3, firmware V2.00", 146 operations), the
storages, the card's objects, and downloads a picture byte for byte as the
card holds it (DSC_0329.JPG, md5 equal to the FAT copy). With d6 set to
the electronic shutter, `ptp.py <socket> capture <dir>` releases the
camera remotely (Nikon InitiateCaptureRecInMedia, 0x9207), waits for the
new object and downloads it. On the camera's screen the first PTP session
brings up the real "upload priority mode" message.

The pieces:

* hw/arm/nikon-z63-dwc3.h (new): the DWC3 at 0x17880000 in device mode,
  ported from the vphone tree's apple-dwc3.c. There it was a QEMU
  USBDevice through a hook its tree added to the USB core; this tree's
  core wants control transfers answered at once, which guest firmware
  cannot do, so the controller takes host tokens directly
  (z63_dwc3_token: SETUP / IN / OUT -> OK / NAK / STALL). Endpoint
  commands, TRB rings in DRAM (0xA1AA09410 + 1040n), the event buffer
  (0xA1AA0C000), the event line on SPI 108 (EXS_USB3_TYPE_C_CONTROLLER;
  ISR sub_40C6C618 masks through GEVNTSIZ and wakes EXSUSBDP,
  sub_40C6C454). This driver numbers hardware endpoints as USB endpoint
  + 1 (sub_40C70950 at 0x40C70A50), so PTP's 0x81/0x02/0x83 are 2/3/4;
  SETEPCONFIG parameter 1 [29:26]/[25] says which USB endpoint each one
  serves. Z63_DWC3_TRACE=1 logs every command, token and event.

* hw/arm/nikon-z63-usbhost.h (new): the host on the other end of the
  cable -- port reset 20 ms after the run bit, control transfers as their
  three stages, bulk until full or short, NAKs retried when an endpoint is
  armed -- and a USB/IP 1.1.1 server in front of it (DEVLIST, IMPORT of
  bus id 1-1, SUBMIT/UNLINK; one client at a time; unix or tcp socket).
  After each reset it reads the descriptors itself and logs
  "Z63_USB: the camera enumerated -- 04b0:0454 ...".

* nikon-z63.c: -machine usbip= and usb-cable= (bool, run-time settable,
  on by default with usbip=). The cable is VBUS on logical pin 0xC8 =
  GPIO port 14 bit 10 (descriptor .data 0xA0280AB38), sampled every 20 ms
  by sub_403204D0, four equal samples to change; its edge starts task
  "USB" (sub_40321D7C). The rest of the start-up needed nothing new: the
  PD-register check through MCU link family 17 is answered by the real
  MCU firmware.

* nikon-z63-usb.h: the DWC3 window moved to nikon-z63-dwc3.h. The Type-C
  assist block's arming write (0x17A40014, mode 0x11/0x15) used to stop
  the machine; it now sets status bit 0 and raises SPI 109 (DECLARED --
  what the block measures is unknown, it answers at once). Its ISR
  (sub_40C717B4) runs on that line, so SPI 109 is the wiring, not the
  0x17A01000 mux. docs/usb-registers.md updated to match.

Three controller bugs found on the way, each from the trace:

1. Enumeration stopped at the first status stage. The ISR masks and
   EXSUSBDP unmasks through GEVNTSIZ on every batch, and the port reset
   the ring's write pointer on any GEVNTSIZ write: each batch's events
   went back to the start of the ring while the driver read on from where
   it was. Only a new size restarts the ring now.

2. GetObject's data phase is a chain of two TRBs (512 KiB, then the
   rest). XferComplete was posted for each finished TRB; on the real part
   a finished TRB is an event only when it ends the transfer (LST, or a
   short OUT packet: XferComplete) or asks for one (IOC:
   XferInProgress). An XferComplete after the first made the driver stall
   both bulk endpoints when the real end came.

3. A second PTP session, seconds after the first, hung on its first
   GET_DESCRIPTOR. DEPSTARTCFG at SET_CONFIGURATION (0x00020509,
   transfer-resource index 2) reset every endpoint, the control pair too,
   in the middle of the status stage: endpoint 1 said XferNotReady(status)
   twice, the driver answered the second in the next session's data stage
   with a zero-length packet, and every control stage after it was one
   behind. The index now says where the reset starts (0 at init, 2 here).

What does not work: only the first remote release of a boot. It is taken
from upload priority mode (live-view state 0xA03D8221C = 4); afterwards
the camera is back in live view (state 2) and the next 0x9207 answers
0x200F after 20 s -- the release (sub_40F903B8, case 2) waits 10 s each
for flags 0x40000000 and 0x100000 on group 0xA03D81618, gets neither, the
capture service returns 32 and the PTP handler (sub_40836588, switch at
0x40836870) maps that to 0x200F. No static setter of 0x40000000 was found.
Shutter-button releases keep working. docs/plan.md lists it, and records
the Wi-Fi scout's findings as a Next item (CYW43455 on SDIO, driven by
Linux; the IPCU is the first gate).

Linux's usbip attach + gphoto2 against usbip=tcp:...:3240 should work and
is not tried.

smoke.sh passes.

